> **3c. V16 — WHAT EXPEDITING COSTS, WHAT IS PRESERVED, HOW THE ORDER STAYS VISIBLE.** SOURCE-DECISION PROCEDURE, EXECUTABLE (codex V16 item 2; V17 [MAJOR] 5): every collection attempt at or after T_pulse and its verdict is appended, in order, to the append-only `_optionA_dev/collection_log.jsonl`; the FIRST verdict that is ACCEPT-* is BINDING — `build_corpus_identity_v18.py` (`705319a53a2f65f24475dc7862583581f54500fd9d80596eeb855d29493f3c56`) refuses any later build whose record, outcome or seed differs from that first logged ACCEPT (`COLLECTION-LOCKED`), so a delayed or repeated collection cannot choose between source states; the log is committed and pushed with the identity (E3 witness). A NIST pulse that becomes authenticable AFTER the first ACCEPT does not reopen it. ADOPTION BINDING (codex V16 item 6, V17 carried): at approval the approved digest is written to the committed file `_optionA_dev/ADOPTED_RULE_SHA256.txt` (exactly one 64-hex line); the builder refuses a `--rule-sha256` that differs from it and refuses if it is absent (`ADOPTION-MISSING` / `-MALFORMED` / `-MISMATCH`); the driver `run_configurations_v2.py` (`32815edf7792452e855d2b186ff30ae1d67f904c3c0d274673c58a9b990ecffe`) reads the same file and refuses an identity whose `rule_sha256` differs (fixtures `test_build_corpus_identity_v18.py` `86b2ac9b17504383fc5340147c14c5af83b16b6d747c832c1a1e6ed2424e9e33`, 5 tests; `test_run_configurations_v2.py` `77c9b62d5e7d4b03f6b8a7c376d79c9d3d351acf8e206058b7792d89fd0f8cd5`, 19 tests). COST: (i) the NIST primary is, in practice, given up — under V15 the fallback could not open before T_pulse + 24 h, so NIST had at least that long to serve a verifying certificate and was checked live at each later build; under V17 NIST is tried live at build time, at or after T_pulse, once, so the seed will almost certainly come from drand, whose BLS proof this lane cannot verify (LIMIT (ii)); the seed's provenance therefore rests on agreement of ≥ 2 of 4 pinned relays, retained and live, not on a signature verified to a pinned root — a weaker provenance, accepted with eyes open; (ii) the V15 signature and its RETRY record become history: one signed commitment whose seed was never drawn, on file forever, and the register will show a V15 signed-then-superseded row; (iii) nothing else — no sample size, floor, bar, exclusion, attempt count, custody or protection rule moves. PRESERVED: V15's bytes and digest, its signature record, the RETRY beacon record, every pin V15 carries except the three files named above. ORDER: the server-side push event (W3) and the nonce (W5) of step (1a) bound the approval record on both sides; MIN_T_SIGN and EXCLUDED_T_PULSE are lower bounds only; the change record carries the timeline (finding 11:01, dispatch 11:06, confirmation 11:08, code 11:12–11:14, this text 11:16, gate, approval, T_pulse) so a reader sees request → authorisation → approval → pulse in that order.
